  "body": "## Result\n\n2303002 / AMR-022-3002, Function Theory Problem 3.2: **already_solved, 0/5**, credited to Fuglede/Carleson and the original Hayman\u2013Lingham Update 3.2.\n\nEvery nonconstant entire harmonic function in dimension n >= 3 has a proper locally polygonal path to infinity along which u tends to positive infinity. The source update already states this result; the imported open triage missed it. No novelty claim.\n\n## Verification\n\nIndependent full source/proof review: PASS. The packet verifies the needed continuous case using Poisson averages, zero-pasted superlevel pieces, nested unbounded-value components and proper polygonal concatenation. It does not confuse an escaping sequence with an entire asymptotic path. The general discontinuous-subharmonic extension, fixed-ray and quantitative-rate claims are outside scope.\n\nAll 3,675 author controls replay exactly; independent review adds 1,667 checks including two PDF hashes. Both use standard-library Python. Source-free portable review explicitly runs 1,665 checks. The full analytic argument is provided separately from these sanity controls.\n\n## Scope\n\nOnly this target folder and its own QUEUE status cell change; turns stay 0/5. Fresh main, author WIP ancestry and every frozen source/proof/review byte are preserved. One draft PR; no raw-source redistribution, merge or release.\n",
